# TRAP: the picture patterns above also match images/, so a new back-cover or
# filler image is ignored on arrival and a fresh clone cannot build the feast
# that references it. Adding one takes
#   git add -f images/<feast>/<file>
# The patterns stay broad on purpose — unused artwork accumulates fast, and
# nobody wants megabytes of it in history by accident.
# Tracked so far: src/libellus/images/borders/, and the three pictures the
# reference feasts actually reference.
repomix-output.xml
.DS_Store
.claude/
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# Never published: names people, quotes correspondence, records half-finished
# reasoning about them. See "Session state" in AGENTS.md. These stay on disk
# locally; anything in them worth publishing is restated in the map issue, in
# docs/adr/ or in CREDITS.md, attributed by role rather than by name.
private-notes.md
*-review.html
lambertus-email-threads.md
lambertus-hintergrund.md
lambert-corrections.md
# HANDOFF.md was retired 2026-08-02 — its live content became the map issue,
# the rest is in docs/adr/, the issues and git history. Still ignored so that a
# stray one can never be committed by accident.
HANDOFF.md

# Python (libellus package)
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# Staged feast builds (rendered TeX + assets + Makefile per feast)
/build/

# Root-level TeX is generated (pre-staging builds landed at the repo root).
/*.tex

# Everything generated at build time — psalm/Magnificat verses, materialized
# inline GABC, decoded data: URI images — now lands under build/.cache/
# (ADR-0024), so /build/ above already covers it. It is deliberately never
# written inside src/libellus/, which in an installed wheel is read-only.

# raw HTML fetched by the EÜ-1980 psalter scrape (delete to re-fetch)
scripts/psalter-german/cache/

# psalter/ has two owners: the private companion repository is checked out over
# it (ADR-0023), and the public-domain Allioli-Arndt is tracked here (ADR-0041).
# So ignore its contents by default and name the public exceptions, rather than
# ignoring the whole directory and force-adding past it — the Einheitsübersetzung
# is © Katholische Bibelanstalt and not redistributable, and `git add -f` is a
# habit that eventually adds the wrong thing.
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose: unanchored, these patterns also swallowed
# tests/fixtures/psalter/, the synthetic probe Psalter the suite resolves
# against — which is committed, and must be, or the suite fails everywhere but
# this working copy.
#
# The `*` matters: a directory that is itself excluded cannot have anything
# re-included from inside it, so each level has to be opened before the next is
# closed again.
/psalter/*
!/psalter/allioli-arndt/

# psalter/tools/ is the companion repository's, and most of it scrapes or reports
# on the Einheitsübersetzung. Only what produced and reviews Allioli-Arndt is
# ours, so it is named file by file rather than opened as a directory.
!/psalter/tools/
/psalter/tools/*
!/psalter/tools/allioli-arndt-review-template.html
!/psalter/tools/scrape_allioli_arndt.py
!/psalter/tools/split_allioli_arndt_review.py

# The Toolchain: LuaHBTeX and gregorio as WebAssembly plus the minimal texmf
# tree, assembled by scripts/toolchain/build.sh. ~80 MB of binaries built from
# pinned upstream releases, so they are reproducible rather than precious.
# ADR-0026 decision 8 makes this a separately versioned GitHub release asset
# eventually — never a tracked directory, on either plan.
/toolchain/
scripts/toolchain/.cache/

# The Electron shell (#60, ADR-0035): node_modules is resolved from
# package.json, /release/ is electron-builder's output directory (kept
# distinct from dist/, which is the Python wheel's own output).
/node_modules/
/release/

# The application's own build output (#91, ADR-0046). What both hosts serve
# under /app/ — `vite build` remakes it from app/index.html and app/src/, and
# copies app/pipeline/ into it verbatim.
/app/dist/
